From: Arctic <arctic@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: The pictures of Windows 11's context menus.

With the visual style's size "Windows 11" every item the system puts in a
context menu has the picture Windows 11 gives it (menuicons.cpp, drawn by
tools/menu-icons.py): the verbs by their name, the default part, the
background's View, Sort by, Refresh, Paste and the views, New, Send to,
the folders' own Properties, Format and Eject, shortcuts and the Recycle
Bin. Open and Edit show the program that does it, a verb's Icon value is
shown as Windows shows it. New's and Send to's icons sit where win32u puts
pictures. ArcticSetMenuIcon gives the same pictures to other modules.
---
